This gives a type error `Property 'course' does not exist on type 'GetValues<"api::race.race", GetNonPopulatableKeys<"api::race.race">>'.ts(2339)`:
```
const races = await strapi.entityService.findMany("api::race.race", {
      populate: {
        course: {
          populate: {
            organiser: true,
          },
        },
      },
      filters: {
        $and: [
          {
            date: { $gte: startOfYear },
          },
          {
            date: { $lte: endOfYear },
          },
        ],
      },
      sort: { date: "asc" },
    });
```

But if I remove `sort: { date: "asc" }` the `course` is typed correctly. Removing filters has no effect.

